WEBVTT

00:35.944 --> 00:39.567
I was suffocating slowly in the broken shell

00:39.587 --> 00:42.910
Drowning in the static of a burning hell But the

00:42.950 --> 00:45.552
console flickered with a sudden bright green

00:45.732 --> 00:48.675
The cleanest set of numbers that I've ever seen I

00:48.735 --> 00:51.718
recognize a radar, I recognize a code A

00:51.758 --> 00:54.040
transmission coming down the cosmic road

00:57.520 --> 00:59.781
I'm punching in the frequency, I'm opening the

00:59.821 --> 01:02.722
mic Sending out a signal through the heavy metal

01:02.742 --> 01:04.943
strike I'm bleeding out the oxygen, the

01:04.963 --> 01:07.844
temperature is low I need you here right now, I

01:07.864 --> 01:11.665
got nowhere else to go

01:12.265 --> 01:17.867
Mayday, mayday, can you hear me in the deep? I'm

01:17.927 --> 01:22.209
caught inside the wreckage and it's playing for

01:22.269 --> 01:28.731
keeps Mayday, mayday, I'm burning up the wire

01:29.532 --> 01:33.814
Come and pull the engine from the atmospheric

01:33.894 --> 01:39.618
fire I receive the telemetry, I'm reading the

01:39.698 --> 01:43.140
line Get here to the dead breach field, we're

01:43.200 --> 01:47.083
running out of time

01:49.826 --> 01:51.987
The radio goes silent, just the hum of the

01:52.027 --> 01:54.288
machine. I'm watching the horizon on the

01:54.328 --> 01:56.470
shattered screen. Then a shadow blocks the

01:56.490 --> 01:59.411
starlight, massive and wide. A heavy rescue

01:59.451 --> 02:02.673
vessel crossing the divide. The airlock hisses

02:02.753 --> 02:05.534
and the blast doors part. I see my anger coming

02:05.595 --> 02:08.036
with a heavy heart. The freight dogs and the

02:08.076 --> 02:09.997
captain stepping through the breach. You

02:10.097 --> 02:12.898
brought the whole family right into my reach.

02:12.918 --> 02:15.260
I'm punching in the frequency, I'm opening the

02:15.320 --> 02:17.803
mic. Sending out a signal through the heavy

02:17.863 --> 02:20.327
metal strike I'm bleeding out the oxygen, the

02:20.367 --> 02:23.071
temperature is low I need you here right now, I

02:23.111 --> 02:30.303
got nowhere else to go Mayday! Mayday! Can you

02:30.323 --> 02:34.606
hear me in the deep? I'm caught inside the

02:34.646 --> 02:39.949
wreckage and it's playing for keeps Mayday!

02:40.049 --> 02:46.153
Mayday! I'm burning up the wire Come and pull the

02:46.333 --> 02:50.996
engine from the atmospheric fire I'll receive

02:51.016 --> 02:56.780
the telemetry I'm reading the line Get here to

02:56.820 --> 03:00.282
the debris field We're running out of time

03:45.464 --> 03:48.046
You didn't leave me in the dark.

03:51.189 --> 03:53.811
You tracked the signal, you found the spark.

03:56.593 --> 03:58.675
The gravity was crushing, the limit was

03:58.735 --> 04:01.057
crossed, but the family arrived before the

04:01.137 --> 04:01.798
engine was lost!

04:05.331 --> 04:10.836
Mayday, mayday, can you hear me in the deep? I'm

04:10.896 --> 04:15.140
caught inside the wreckage and it's playing for

04:15.180 --> 04:21.686
keeps Mayday, mayday, I'm burning up the wire

04:22.367 --> 04:26.550
Come and pull the engine from the atmospheric

04:26.630 --> 04:32.254
fire I receive the telemetry I'm reading the

04:32.374 --> 04:35.797
line. Get here to the debris field. We're

04:35.837 --> 04:38.939
running out of time.

04:41.481 --> 04:43.683
You read the line.

04:47.205 --> 04:52.910
You made the time. Cavalry is here.

